.TH shuf 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
shuf \- generate random permutations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY shuf
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE ]
.YS
.SY shuf
.BI \-e
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ ARG \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SY shuf
.BI \-i \~LO-HI
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Write a random permutation of the input lines to standard output.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#shuf\-e
\fB\-e, \-\-echo\fP
.UE
treat each ARG as an input line
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#shuf\-i
\fB\-i, \-\-input\-range=\,LO\-HI\fP
.UE
treat each number LO through HI as an input line
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#shuf\-n
\fB\-n, \-\-head\-count=\,COUNT\fP
.UE
output at most COUNT lines
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#shuf\-o
\fB\-o, \-\-output=\,FILE\fP
.UE
write result to FILE instead of standard output
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#shuf\-\-random\-source
\fB\-\-random\-source=FILE\fP
.UE
get random bytes from FILE
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#shuf\-r
\fB\-r, \-\-repeat\fP
.UE
output lines can be repeated
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#shuf\-z
\fB\-z, \-\-zero\-terminated\fP
.UE
line delimiter is NUL, not newline
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/shuf#shuf\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/shuf#shuf\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
